End the Schannel copy loop when close_notify arrives along with data.
tls_read marks the session closed when DecryptMessage reports the peer's
close_notify, but if data was decrypted earlier in the same call it
returns that data, and the copy loop wrote it and went back to poll().
Nothing more would ever arrive, so a server that waits for the client's
close_notify before closing the connection left ssl_client, and wget
reading a body without Content-Length through it, hanging until the
server timed out or standard input ended. After writing the data, end
the session if tls_read found it closed.

---
 networking/tls.c |    6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/networking/tls.c
+++ b/networking/tls.c
@@ -3703,11 +3703,13 @@
 		}
 		if (pfds[1].revents) {
 			nread = tls_read(tls, buffer, sizeof(buffer));
-			if (nread < 1) {
+			if (nread > 0)
+				xwrite(STDOUT_FILENO, buffer, nread);
+			/* the peer's close_notify may arrive along with data */
+			if (nread < 1 || tls->connection_state != BB_SCHANNEL_OPEN) {
 				tls_disconnect(tls);
 				break;
 			}
-			xwrite(STDOUT_FILENO, buffer, nread);
 		}
 	}
 }
